// Secrets.xcconfig.template — NovaPresence Zoom configuration TEMPLATE.
//
// Copy this file to "Secrets.xcconfig" in this same folder and fill the
// values LOCALLY, or create matching GitHub Secrets and let CI generate
// the file. Secrets.xcconfig is git-ignored. NEVER commit a filled copy,
// never paste real values into any other file, issue, log, or chat.
//
// KEY NAMES ONLY — the values below are intentionally blank:
//
//   VIDEO_SDK_KEY              Zoom Video SDK — SDK Key
//                              (Phase-2 development SANDBOX only. Video SDK
//                              sessions are NOT Zoom meetings.)
//   VIDEO_SDK_SECRET_PRESENT   Set to YES in the real Secrets.xcconfig only
//                              as a marker that the Video SDK secret is held
//                              by the (future) token-signing step. Do NOT put
//                              the raw Video SDK secret in the app bundle:
//                              Zoom's own guidance is that SDK secrets are
//                              used server-side to sign join tokens, never
//                              embedded in client code.
//   MEETING_SDK_KEY            Zoom Meeting SDK — Client ID / SDK Key
//                              (the production route to real Zoom meetings;
//                              Custom UI mode. Wired in a later phase.)
//   MEETING_SDK_SECRET_PRESENT Same rule as above: marker only, YES/NO.
//                              The raw secret never ships in the app.
//
// In GitHub, the corresponding repository secrets are named:
//   ZOOM_VIDEO_SDK_KEY
//   ZOOM_VIDEO_SDK_SECRET
//   ZOOM_MEETING_SDK_KEY
//   ZOOM_MEETING_SDK_SECRET
// The workflow only checks whether they EXIST (true/false) for the build
// log; it does not print them and this Phase-2 build does not embed the
// secrets themselves into the app.

VIDEO_SDK_KEY =
VIDEO_SDK_SECRET_PRESENT = NO
MEETING_SDK_KEY =
MEETING_SDK_SECRET_PRESENT = NO
